      "math_academy_id": "q-126176",
      "sequence_position": 20,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}0, & x<4 \\\\ 1-\\frac{16}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X>6).$",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =1-P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =1-F(6) \\\\  & =1-(1-\\frac{16}{{6}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
